     },
     "updated": "2018-09-07T15:20:18.244-0300"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This could be a question of best practices. But I am seeing no use for the acl:accessToClass predicate without an acl:default in the same acl:Authorization. Maybe what I am suggesting is we code a best practice into the implementation and maybe that is a bad idea? But I really don't see why you use acl:accessToClass to refer to a single specific resource which is how our WebAC implementation works without an acl:default predicate.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "This seemed more problematic when discussing with ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
           "text": "@Aaron Birkland"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " and ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
           "text": "@Peter Matthew Eichman"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " yesterday. But I am fine letting people use acl:accessToClass however they want, I'm just thinking people may expect this to work differently than it will.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "If ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae",
           "text": "@Aaron Birkland"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " and ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
           "text": "@Peter Matthew Eichman"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " don't have a good reason, then I'm good with closing this and letting the cats run un-herded.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
