  "customfield_10045": null,
  "customfield_10047": null,
  "customfield_10048": null,
  "customfield_10049": null,
  "customfield_10050": null,
  "customfield_10051": null,
  "customfield_10052": null,
  "customfield_10053": null,
  "customfield_10054": null,
  "customfield_10087": null,
  "customfield_10121": null,
  "customfield_10154": null,
  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ],
       "text": "The task here is to clarify the best practice in the documentation.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Because of the way that acl:default takes the ACL and re-writes it onto child objects, then any object that is underneath gets the same permissions.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Because you would need the parent object to have the class defined in the acl:accessToClass, then why not specify acl:accessTo.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "If instead you use acl:default and acl:accessToClass, then this seems to be a method to assign these permissions to a subset of the children (those with the specified class).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "ie.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "/rest/trunk",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<> a pcdm-use:Image",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "/rest/trunk/fcr:acl",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " <> a webac:Acl .",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": " <#auth1> a acl:Authorization ;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "    acl:accessToClass pcdm-use:Image ;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "    acl:mode acl:Read ;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "    acl:agent \"somebody\" ;",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "    acl:default </rest/trunk> .",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Then any child item that shares the type pcdm-use:Image would get these authorizations, others would continue up the tree.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
