  "comment": {
   "comments": [
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Bernstein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" data-account-id=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" accountid=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Jared Whiklo</a>:  Is this a problem? Are you suggesting we return a 400 with a descriptive warning?  </p>",
     "created": "07/Sep/18 3:20 PM",
     "id": "20177",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12798/comment/20177",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3707b443358c8c223f9eec7a7d29ba88?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FDB-4.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Danny Bernstein",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "07/Sep/18 3:20 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>This could be a question of best practices. But I am seeing no use for the acl:accessToClass predicate without an acl:default in the same acl:Authorization. Maybe what I am suggesting is we code a best practice into the implementation and maybe that is a bad idea? But I really don't see why you use acl:accessToClass to refer to a single specific resource which is how our WebAC implementation works without an acl:default predicate.</p>\n\n<p>This seemed more problematic when discussing with <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" data-account-id=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" accountid=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Aaron Birkland</a> and <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" data-account-id=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" accountid=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Peter Matthew Eichman</a> yesterday. But I am fine letting people use acl:accessToClass however they want, I'm just thinking people may expect this to work differently than it will.</p>\n\n<p>If <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" data-account-id=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" accountid=\"5ed02cb2dacd410c1f9e56ae\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Aaron Birkland</a> and <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3A4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" data-account-id=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" accountid=\"557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Peter Matthew Eichman</a> don't have a good reason, then I'm good with closing this and letting the cats run un-herded.</p>",
     "created": "07/Sep/18 4:22 PM",
     "id": "20179",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12798/comment/20179",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/45c30a3354c38331cc42d11962474554?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FJW-1.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Jared Whiklo",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "updated": "07/Sep/18 4:22 PM"
    },
    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/be7c7dc994e3e4d444fe0c6473628654?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FPE-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Peter Matthew Eichman",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>My current feeling on this is that we should not enforce this in the implementation, but instead make it clear in a best practices document that authorizations with <tt>acl:accessToClass</tt> without <tt>acl:default</tt> are likely to be useless, or not be doing what you think you are doing. (Until, of course, someone comes along with a strange edge case where it <b>does</b> make sense <img class=\"emoticon\" src=\"/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png\" height=\"16\" width=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\"/>)</p>",
     "created": "12/Sep/18 3:37 PM",
     "id": "20197",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12798/comment/20197",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "557058:4cbd1cac-35ff-460e-a296-7f84d2cbc967",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
